@@ -96,6 +96,9 @@ Bugs
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.PhysionetMI` failing in every paradigm call that mixes subjects 88, 92 or 100 with other subjects: these three subjects were recorded at 128 Hz (every imagery and execution run) and the other 106 at 160 Hz, so ``LeftRightImagery().get_data(PhysionetMI(), subjects=[1, 88])`` stopped in ``np.concatenate`` ("the array at index 0 has size 481 and the array at index 6 has size 385") and ``return_epochs=True`` in ``concatenate_epochs`` ("epochs[6].info['sfreq'] must match"); the docstring only mentioned subject 88. The loader now resamples any run that is not at 160 Hz to 160 Hz, so all 109 subjects load together. Cached epochs and saved results that include subjects 88, 92 or 100 must be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`1280` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix the BigP3BCI loaders (:class:`moabb.datasets.Mainsah2025_A` to :class:`moabb.datasets.Mainsah2025_S2`) returning slightly different sampling rates from run to run (e.g. 256.0, 256.00008 and 256.00009 Hz within one subject): every EDF stores the run as one data record whose 8-character duration field is truncated, so the rate MNE derives from the header is off by less than 1 ppm and differs per file. Arrays were unaffected, but ``return_epochs=True`` (and anything concatenating epochs, e.g. deep-learning pipelines) stopped with "epochs[3].info['sfreq'] must match" even for a single subject. Runs whose header rate is explained by this truncation are now relabelled at exactly 256 Hz (no resampling; the samples are unchanged), and any other rate raises. Cached ``Mainsah2025-*`` epochs computed before this fix carry the per-file rates and should be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`XXXX` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix the BigP3BCI loaders (:class:`moabb.datasets.Mainsah2025_A` to :class:`moabb.datasets.Mainsah2025_S2`) returning slightly different sampling rates from run to run (e.g. 256.0, 256.00008 and 256.00009 Hz within one subject): every EDF stores the run as one data record whose 8-character duration field is truncated, so the rate MNE derives from the header is off by less than 1 ppm and differs per file. Arrays were unaffected, but ``return_epochs=True`` (and anything concatenating epochs, e.g. deep-learning pipelines) stopped with "epochs[3].info['sfreq'] must match" even for a single subject. Runs whose header rate is explained by this truncation are now relabelled at exactly 256 Hz (no resampling; the samples are unchanged), and any other rate raises. Cached ``Mainsah2025-*`` epochs computed before this fix carry the per-file rates and should be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`1281` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- :class:`moabb.datasets.Ofner2017` returns the same channel names in the same order for every run, which ``return_all_modalities`` needs: subject 1's execution runs store the EOG channels as eog-r, eog-m, eog-l (all other runs: eog-l, eog-m, eog-r), so arrays with EOG swapped eog-l and eog-r, and its imagination runs hold 13 placeholder channels ``armeodummy-0``..``armeodummy-12`` (random values) instead of the Armeo arm-kinematics channels; ``MotorImagery().get_data(Ofner2017(return_all_modalities=True), subjects=[1], return_epochs=True)`` failed with "epochs[10].info['ch_names'] must match". The EOG channels are now reordered by name and the placeholders renamed to the Armeo names and set to 0, like the (empty) Armeo channels of the other runs; ``METADATA`` lists the Armeo names. The default EEG-only output is unchanged. Cached Ofner2017 epochs and results computed with ``return_all_modalities`` must be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`XXXX` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
